From d3b42fa007a61dcff264b0159a89f08c1e24aa33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:27:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Reuse guarded replica readers in dispatcher operator
 and wake scans

G2b live proof still costs .903% core; profiles attribute remaining drain cost to guarded opens. Borrow the bounded generation-aware reader exclusively, fallback on contention, preserve Row/5s timeout and release transactions on all exits. Keep general foreign_card close-on-exit contract unchanged.

Proof: three baseline RED cases; 84 focused contracts green plus 42 operator cases. Five exact mutants killed. Real drain replica scale replay (1k/5.8k/20k live tasks, 10k/40k replica tasks, 512 extra FDs, checkpointed and 425MB WAL) cuts ~2.8-4.5ms to .43-.56ms/tick; equal executor clocks. Synthetic idle incoming workload, not live whole-reclaim acceptance. Hub P1 >=360s remains mandatory after deployment.
